window.docContents[39].resolve({"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.Assumptions.Assumptions/#file-Computational___Specifications___Assumptions___Assumptions":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/Assumptions › Assumptions.leanTier 1 · statement file\n\nTier 1 · statement file used by the computational proof 1 headline theorem depend on it 315 lines trust banner B1, trusted: the statement source ↗Read in full. A statement file: its definitions say what the headline theorems claim (games, adversaries, bounds). Proofs are cut after := and shown as ⋯; Lean checks them.\n\nDeclarations on this page (29)inductive PrimQuerydef primSpecdef primImplabbrev PrimBaseSpecdef isPrimQuerydef isPrimQuery₀def primBaseImplabbrev DdhQuerydef gapDhOracleSpecinductive SigQuerydef sigOracleSpecdef sigAndDdhSpecdef isSigChalQuerydef isDdhChalQuerystructure GapDhWithSignAdvdef GapDhWithSignAdv.Boundeddef gapDhWithSignExpdef GapDhWithSignstructure KemShCrAdvdef KemShCrAdv.Boundeddef kemShCrExpdef KemShCrstructure GapSigEufCmaAdvdef GapSigEufCmaAdv.Boundeddef gapSigEufCmaExpdef GapSigEufCmadef primQueryBudgetdef gdhQueryBudgetdef gdhPrimQueryBudget\n\n\n\nCryptographic assumption games and the primitive oracle for PQXDHTrusted: the statement. The assumption games (GapDhWithSign, GapSigEufCma, KemShCr), their adversary types, the .Bounded predicates, the primitive oracle primSpec, the combined challenger oracle sigAndDdhSpec, and the budgets primQueryBudget / gdhPrimQueryBudget / gdhQueryBudget are used by the statement (Security/Headline.lean, Security/HeadlineDelta.lean, StatementPqElf.lean). The standalone two-key and Auth assumptions (GapDH, SigEufCma, AeadIndCpa, PrfHmac, PrfChainKey, PrfMsgKeys) are in Computational/Proofs/SignalPqxdh/TwoKeyAndAuthStatements.lean, and the remaining auxiliary assumptions (KemIndCca, HkdfRO, RootKdfRO, AeadIntCtxt, AeadMuIntCtxt, PrfRk, HkdfPRF, IkTwoKeyIdealisation, CryptoWellFormedPrimitives) are in Computational/Proofs/SpecLemmas/SignalPqxdh/Assumptions.lean, both checked by Lean. See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.Each assumption game is a ProbComp Bool experiment over P : Primitives against an adversary carrying declared query budgets q_* enforced by .Bounded. Assumption adversaries evaluate P through the primitive oracle primSpec (counted by q_prim), whereas the X25519 decisional Diffie-Hellman oracle isValidDhTriple is exposed on the challenger interface sigAndDdhSpec (counted by q_ddh).GapDhWithSign (DEV-PQ17) and GapSigEufCma model libsignal's reuse of a single Curve25519 identity scalar across X25519 Diffie-Hellman and XEdDSA pre-key signing (Perrin, 2016; Degabriele et al., CT-RSA 2012; Thormarker, ePrint 2021/509; Brendel et al., IEEE S&P 2021): in the SHA-512 random-oracle model, a Schnorr simulator guessing the key-fixed Edwards sign bit in sig[63] reduces GapDhWithSign to standalone GapDH within a factor of 2, and forking-lemma reductions reduce GapSigEufCma to discrete logarithm given the DDH oracle. KemShCr models semi-honest collision resistance of Kyber-1024 (Bhargavan, Jacomme, Kiefer, Schmidt, USENIX Security 2024, Def. 1 and Thm. 5).\n\n\n\nPrimitive oracle\n\ninductive PrimQueryL56–77 ↗#Queries to the primitive oracle, with one constructor per Primitives operation used by the handshake and session games (excluding isValidDhTriple and internal leaf primitives).\n\ndef primSpecL79–98 ↗#\n\ndef primImplL100–120 ↗#Evaluates primSpec queries deterministically using P.\n\nabbrev PrimBaseSpecL122–124 ↗#Base oracle interface for assumption adversaries: uniform sampling plus primSpec, with game-specific challenger oracles added on the right.\n\ndef isPrimQueryL126–128 ↗#\n\ndef isPrimQuery₀L130–132 ↗#\n\ndef primBaseImplL134–135 ↗#\n\nSigning and DDH challenger oracles\n\nabbrev DdhQueryL139–140 ↗#Decisional Diffie-Hellman query (X, Y, Z) testing pow8(Z) = CDH_subG(pow8(X), pow8(Y)).\n\ndef gapDhOracleSpecL142 ↗#\n\ninductive SigQueryL144–146 ↗#\n\ndef sigOracleSpecL148 ↗#\n\ndef sigAndDdhSpecL150–153 ↗#Combined XEdDSA signing and X25519 DDH challenger interface shared by GapDhWithSign and GapSigEufCma.\n\ndef isSigChalQueryL155–157 ↗#\n\ndef isDdhChalQueryL159–161 ↗#\n\nGapDhWithSign\n\nstructure GapDhWithSignAdvL165–171 ↗#Adversary for single-pair X25519 Gap-DH with an XEdDSA signing oracle on the first challenge key U = P.x25519Base u (DEV-PQ17), carrying query budgets q_ddh, q_sig, and q_prim.\n\ndef GapDhWithSignAdv.BoundedL173–177 ↗#Every run of A respects its declared q_ddh, q_sig, and q_prim query budgets.\n\ndef gapDhWithSignExpL179–195 ↗#Single-pair X25519 Gap-DH experiment with signing oracle on u: samples scalars u and v, gives (P.x25519Base u, P.x25519Base v) to A with randomized XEdDSA signing under u and DDH oracle isValidDhTriple, and checks pow8 Z = pow8 (P.x25519 u V).\n\ndef GapDhWithSignL197–201 ↗#Success probability of A in gapDhWithSignExp (DEV-PQ17).\n\nKemShCr\n\nstructure KemShCrAdvL205–211 ↗#Two-stage adversary for Kyber-1024 semi-honest collision resistance (BJKS24 Def. 1), with per-stage primitive-oracle budget q_prim.\n\ndef KemShCrAdv.BoundedL213–219 ↗#Both stages of A make at most A.q_prim primitive-oracle queries.\n\ndef kemShCrExpL221–232 ↗#Kyber-1024 semi-honest collision-resistance experiment (BJKS24 Def. 1): A.choosePk receives an honest key pair (pk, sk) and outputs (pk', st); given an honest encapsulation (ss, ct) under pk', A.findCollision wins by outputting ct' with P.kemDecaps sk ct' = some ss, ct' ≠ ct ∨ pk' ≠ pk, ct'.length = kyberCtLen, and pk'.length = kyberPkLen.\n\ndef KemShCrL234–236 ↗#Success probability of A in kemShCrExp.\n\nGapSigEufCma\n\nstructure GapSigEufCmaAdvL240–246 ↗#Adversary for XEdDSA EUF-CMA security in the presence of the X25519 DDH oracle, carrying query budgets q_sig, q_ddh, and q_prim.\n\ndef GapSigEufCmaAdv.BoundedL248–252 ↗#Every run of A respects its declared q_sig, q_ddh, and q_prim query budgets.\n\ndef gapSigEufCmaExpL254–271 ↗#XEdDSA EUF-CMA experiment with DDH oracle isValidDhTriple: gives pk = P.sigPkGen sk to A, answers signing queries under sk with fresh 64-byte randomness while recording queried messages, and checks that (m*, sig*) verifies on an unqueried m*.\n\ndef GapSigEufCmaL273–276 ↗#Success probability of A in gapSigEufCmaExp.\n\n\n\nReduction query budgets\n\ndef primQueryBudgetL282–286 ↗#Specification primitive-oracle budget for an assumption adversary built from a game adversary with budget b: 16 * (5 * N_dh + N_sess_tot + 12) primitive calls per game query plus one final extraction pass.\n\ndef gdhQueryBudgetL288–297 ↗#DDH-oracle budget of the GapDhWithSign and GapSigEufCma reductions for game budget b: random-oracle × session consistency checks (4 * M_ro * M_sess) plus distinct session-pair checks (2 * M_sess * (M_sess - 1)), capped at 4 * q_total^2, plus q_total + N_dh + N_sess_tot for final extraction (M_sess is bounded by q_on since only online queries create sessions).\n\ndef gdhPrimQueryBudgetL299–305 ↗#Sharper primitive-oracle budget for the one-key GapDhWithSign and GapSigEufCma reductions: charges the full per-query cost 16 * (5 * N_dh + N_sess_tot + 12) only to the at most M_sess = min (min q_on q_total) N_sess_tot online session queries (plus final extraction), and 32 to every other game query.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/Assumptions/Assumptions.lean","id":"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.Assumptions.Assumptions/#file-Computational___Specifications___Assumptions___Assumptions"},"/Tier-2___-definitions/LibsignalBinary___Specifications___/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.CryptoGames.SM.Construction/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___CryptoGames___SM___Construction":{"contents":"Paper › LibsignalBinary/Specifications/CryptoGames/SM › Construction.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the computational proof 1 headline theorem depend on it 27 of 157 lines trusted trust banner B3, trusted in part source ↗Read the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nThe Signal-based SM scheme (ACD19 Fig. 8)Trusted in part. The theorems of Computational/Theorems/ use only the types Header and PartyState from this file: read them. initParty, send, receive, scheme and the theorems here are checked by Lean. See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.Generic secure-messaging scheme of ACD19 §5.1 (Alwen, Coretti, Dodis, ePrint 2018/1037) built from a continuous key agreement scheme cka, a root PRF-PRNG prng, and a per-epoch FS-AEAD scheme fs (Ratchet/LibsignalSMInstance.lean instantiates it for libsignal).\n\n\n\nabbrev HeaderL35–42 ↗#Message header h = (t, T_t) (T = none encodes λ in epoch 0), passed as FS-AEAD associated data.DEV-SM11 (formalization): no FS-Stop, FS-Max or ℓ_prv. ACD19 Fig. 8 sends ℓ_prv so the receiver can erase old sessions via FS-Max and FS-Stop. Here old sessions are retained, the header is (t, T), and old-epoch forgeries are handled in the SM game (DEV-SM7; see DEV-LS13 for libsignal's previous_counter).\n\nstructure PartyStateL44–62 ↗#Per-party state for ACD19 Fig. 8.\n\n4 declarations not shown (lines 71–153): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesCryptoGames.SM.Construction.initParty, CryptoGames.SM.Construction.send, CryptoGames.SM.Construction.receive, CryptoGames.SM.Construction.scheme\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"LibsignalBinary/Specifications/CryptoGames/SM/Construction.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/LibsignalBinary___Specifications___/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.CryptoGames.SM.Construction/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___CryptoGames___SM___Construction"}});